    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0847" n="1681" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/818</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-08T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1101. Embassy’s 1301, May 4, 1 p.m.; 1302, May 4, 8 p.m.;<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d729-f1"/> and 1303, May 4, 10 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d729-f2"/>
                    The Department and the War Trade Board have considered the views expressed in
                    the above-mentioned cablegrams and in accordance with your recommendation it has
                    been determined that this Government will extend the provisions of article 13 of
                    the commercial agreement of March 7, 1918, for an additional period of 31 days;
                    that is, General Rules No. 1 governing the granting of licenses for
                        bunkers<anchor n="2" xml:id="d729-f3"/> will not be applied to Spanish
                    vessels during the period ending June 8, 1918, during which period the present
                    regulations will remain in force.</p>
                <p>As requested in Embassy’s 1302 (No. 50 from Chadbourne to War Trade Board)
                    the Department has not communicated this decision to the Spanish Ambassador in
                    Washington and you should immediately notify the Foreign Office of the 31-day
                    extension of article 13. At the same time you should state that every effort is
                    being made by this Government to expedite the institution of the tonnage
                    negotiations and that it is fully expected that within the next day or two the
                    United States shipping expert will proceed to Madrid with full instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
